{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For what great nation is there that has gods close to it.</b> The reason it is fitting to insist that you be accounted wise and understanding in the eyes of the nations, is that the blessed Elohim is close to us whenever we call to Him. This indicates that He chose us from among all the peoples. And if the nations account you fools, it will be a profanation of HaShem, as it says: לְכָל עַם ה׳ אֵלֶּה (Ezekiel 36:20)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:21.542927742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}